      <div type="clause" n="El. 21">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 21</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 21" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="32" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif oxa ofhnite wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.37"/> oððe wíf, þæt hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.38"/> dead sien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.39"/>, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.11"/> he mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.40"/>, ⁊ ne sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.41"/> his flæsc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.42"/> eten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.43"/>; se hlaford<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.star2"/> bið unscyldig. Gif se oxa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.star3"/> hnitol wære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.44"/> twam dagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ǽr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="45" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.45"/> oððe ðrim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="46" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.46"/>, ⁊ se hlaford hit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.dagger"/> wisse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="47" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.47"/> ⁊ hine inne betynan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="48" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.48"/> nolde, ⁊ he ðonne wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.44"/> oððe wíf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="49" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.49"/> ofsloge, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.1"/> he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.2"/> mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.3"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.star"/>, ⁊ sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.1"/> se hlaford ófslegen oððe forgolden, swa ðæt witan to ryhte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.4"/> finden.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.5"/> Sunu oððe dohtor gif he ofstinge, ðæs ilcan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.6"/> domes sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.1"/> he wyrðe. Gif he ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> ðeow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.7"/> oððe ðeowmennen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.8"/> ófstinge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.9"/>, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.10"/> þam hlaforde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.11"/> XXX scill. seolfres, ⁊ se oxa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.star2"/> mid stanum ofworpod.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.star"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 21" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="32" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf oxa ofhnite wer oððe wif, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hie dead sien, sie he mid stanum ofworpod, ⁊ ne sie his flæsc éten. Se hlaford bið unscyldig, gif se oxa hnitol wære twam dagum oððe þrim ǽr, ⁊ sé hlaford hit nyste. Gif he hit ðonne wiste ⁊ he hine betynan nolde, ⁊ he ðonne wer oððe wif ofsloge, sy he mid stanum ofworpod, ⁊ sie se hlaford ofslagen oððe forgolden, swa þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> witan to rihte findan. Sunu oððe dohtor gyf he ofstinge, sy he þæs ylcan domes wyrðe. Gif he þonne ðeow oððe ðeowne ofstinge, gesylle ðam hlaforde XXX scill' seolfres, ⁊ se oxa sie mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpad.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 21" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="33" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif oxa ofhnite wer oððe wif, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hy deade syn, sy he mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> oftorfod, ⁊ ne sy his flæsc geeten; se hlaford byð unscyldig. Gif se oxa hnitol wære twam dagum ær oððe þrym, ⁊ se hlaford hit wiste ⁊ hine innan betynan nolde, ⁊ he þonne wer oððe wif ofsloge, sy he mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpen, ⁊ sy se hlaford ofslegen oððe se man forgolden, swa þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wytan to rihte fyndaþ. Sunu oððe dohter gif he stynge, þæs ilcan domes sy he wyrðe. Gyf he þonne þeowan oððe þeowene ofstynge, gesylle þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> hlaforde þryttig scll' seolfres, ⁊ sy se oxa mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 21" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="33" ed="#liebermann"/>Si bos cornu petierit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.11-2"/> uirum aut mulierem, et mortui fuerint, lapidibus obruetur, et non comedentur carnes eius; dominus quoque bouis innocens erit. Quodsi bos cornupeta fuerit ab heri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.1-2"/> et nudiustercius, et contestati sunt dominum eius, nec reclusit eum, occideritque uirum aut mulierem, et bos lapidibus obruetur, et dominum illius occident. Quodsi pretium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.2-2"/> ei fuerit impositum, dabit pro anima sua quicquid fuerit postulatus. Filium quoque et filiam si cornu petierit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.3-2"/>, simili sententiæ subiacebit. Si seruum ancillamque inuaserit, triginta siclos argenti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.4-2"/> dabit domino suo, bos uero lapidibus opprimetur.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.oe.5-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 21" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="244" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif oxa ofhnite wer oððe wif, þæt hie dead sien, sie he mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpod, ⁊ ne sie his flæsc eten; se hlaford bið unscyldig. Gif se oxa hnitol wære twam dagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ær oððe ðrim, ⁊ se hlaford hit wisse ⁊ hine inne betynan nolde, ⁊ he ðonne wer oððe wif ofsloge, sie he mid stanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ofworpod, ⁊ sie se hlaford ófslegen oððe forgolden, swa ðæt witan to ryhte finden. Sunu oððe dohtor gif he ofstinge, ðæs ilcan domes sie he wyrðe. Gif he ðonne ðeow oððe ðeowmennen ofstinge, geselle þam hlaforde XXX scill seolfres, ⁊ se oxa mid stanum ofworpod.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="33" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.1"/> ein Ochs Mann oder Weib stösst, dass sie todt sind, werde er mit Steinen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.2"/> todtgeworfen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.3"/>, und sein Fleisch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.4"/> werde nicht gegessen; der Herr ist<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.5"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de1.star2"/> unschuldig.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.6"/> Wenn der Ochs stössig war an zwei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.7"/> Tagen vorher oder an dreien, und der Herr es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.5"/> wusste und ihn nicht drinnen einschliessen wollte, und der nun Mann oder Weib getödtet hat, so werde der [Ochs] mit Steinen todt geworfen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.8"/>, und der Herr werde getödtet oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.9"/> losgekauft, wie das die [Gerichts-]Oberen zu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.10"/> Recht finden. Wenn der [Ochs dem Nachbar] Sohn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.11"/> oder Tochter todt stösst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.12"/>, sei er [der Herr] desselben Urtheiles theilhaftig. Wenn jener [Ochs] jedoch Sklaven oder Sklavin<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.13"/> todt stösst, zahle er [sein Herr] dem Herrn [jener] 30 Schill. Silbers<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.14"/>, und werde der Ochs mit Steinen todtgeworfen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-21.lnote.de.15"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If an ox gores a man or a woman so that they are dead, let it be stoned to death, and let its flesh not be eaten; the owner is innocent. If the ox was given to goring two days before or three, and the owner knew it and would not shut it in, and it has now killed a man or a woman, then let [the ox] be stoned to death, and let the owner be killed or redeemed, as the [judicial] authorities find to be right. If [the ox] gores to death [a neighbour’s] son or daughter, let him [the owner] be subject to the same judgment. But if that [ox] gores to death a slave or a slave woman, let him [its owner] pay the master [of those] 30 shillings of silver, and let the ox be stoned to death.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="245" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If an ox should gore a man or woman, so that they die, let it be slain by stoning, and let its flesh not be eaten; the lord will be guiltless. If the ox was given to pushing with its horns two or three days before, and the lord knew of it and did not wish to enclose him, and it then killed a man or woman, let it be slain by stoning, and let the lord be slain or paid for, as the assembly may deem right. If it gore a son or daughter, let him be worthy of the same judgment. If, however, it should gore a male or female slave, let the lord give thirty silver shillings and the ox be killed by stoning.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 21,28–32</note>
